Removed the `max_num` check and use a single initialization flag; returning `lookup[num]` directly is equivalent because the table is zero-initialized. This saves one branch and one load per call.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const Profile::MESG* lookup[65536] = {};
    static bool initialized = false;

    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; i++)
        {
            FIT_UINT16 n = mesgs[i].num;
            if (lookup[n] == NULL)
                lookup[n] = &mesgs[i];
        }
        initialized = true;
    }

    return lookup[num];
}
```